        "evidence": "Proof sketch: 'By flatness, closed loops encircling separated subsets have commuting holonomies. ... The scalar obstruction requires non-abelian monodromy, **which flatness rules out**.' Also 'Flatness is **equivalent to** semisimplicity of the braided tensor category' and 'Each crossing multiplies mass by $\\approx 94$'.",
